{"id":"signature-dates-vs-meeting","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"What the posted papers show of signing before the vote","question":"Were these contracts signed before the board voted on them, as far as the posted copies show?","finding":"The posted copies show little of signing. Of 274 contract and amendment papers, 24 carry a typed or stamped signature date (24 before the meeting); other signatures are handwritten or blank and were not dated here. 63 of the 65 that are “dated for convenience” carry a date before the meeting, which is the drafting date, not a signature. Where the signature block has the line “approved/ratified by the Board of Education on”, it is blank in 37 of 39 papers read; 2 have a board date written in, and in 1 of those it is not the meeting the paper is posted for.","how":"Typed signature dates: \"Date:\" or \"Signed:\" followed by a date, leaving out the school-site plan forms (\"School Site Name\"). \"Dated for convenience\" dates from the opening line. The board-date line is read from the signature block. OCR text is used for scans.","limits":"A posted copy is often the contractor-signed copy sent for approval, so a contractor signature before the vote is the normal order; the district’s officers sign after the board acts. Handwritten dates in scans were not read. A blank board-date line shows the posted copy was not completed, not that the contract was unsigned.","columns":[{"k":"meeting","t":"Meeting","type":"date"},{"k":"vendor","t":"Vendor","type":"org"},{"k":"doc","t":"Paper","type":"text"},{"k":"signed","t":"Typed signature date","type":"date"},{"k":"dated","t":"Dated for convenience","type":"date"},{"k":"board","t":"Board date in the signature block","type":"text"},{"k":"link","t":"Attachment","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"meeting":"2018-01-09","vendor":"SAP","vendorKey":null,"doc":"EXECUTED SAP ORDER FORM for HCM Cloud Services FOR BOARD of EDUCATION approval F","signed":"2017-12-27","dated":null,"board":"not read","link":{"t":"BoardDocs 